# Defaults for `npm run dev`. Committed on purpose — nothing here is a secret,
# and every value is a localhost address.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#   `npm run dev` used to start with no SOFA_PROXY_URL, so /api/sofa skipped
#   the local proxy entirely and served whatever was in the blob cache. The
#   board then looked broken in a way that pointed at the wrong thing: fixtures
#   hours old, or an empty page, with a working data feed running on port 3001
#   the whole time. Only ./run-local.sh set this, so the app behaved differently
#   depending on which command you happened to type.
#
# Next.js precedence: .env.local overrides this file, so setting either of
# these there still wins for anyone who wants something different.

# The local SofaScore proxy — the launchd agent `in.tennisalpha.sofa-proxy`,
# or `python sofa_proxy.py` in a spare terminal. Without it the board has no
# live source at all; with it, scores and schedules come straight from upstream.
SOFA_PROXY_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3001
